1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Welcome to MSBA Job Matching, a grounded decision-support system for career advisors.
This demo runs a normal search, two edge cases, and the measured evaluation.

2
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:38,000
The router separates search requests from postings. Search mode applies hard constraints;
posting mode classifies fit. Calibrated policy gates produce evidence, actions, and review reasons.

3
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:56,000
This real request asks for entry-level US analytics roles using SQL, Python, Excel,
Tableau, or Power BI. The system preserves the input as search mode.

4
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:26,000
The output returns compliant job evidence without inventing a posting label for the query.
A six-query audit found zero hard-constraint violations and zero duplicate company-title pairs.

5
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:44,000
This edge case is a strong analytics match, but its source text explicitly says no OPT or CPT.
Role fit and authorization must remain separate decisions.

6
00:01:44,000 --> 00:02:14,000
The classifier preserves high fit, while the explicit restriction forces review and a Hold action.
The system never turns role relevance into an immigration, eligibility, or hiring decision.

7
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:38,000
This posting lacks company, location, country, and schedule fields. The completeness gate
overrides medium fit to unclear and routes the case to review.

8
00:02:38,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Macro F1 is 98.4% on the fixed set and 97.6% on the newest 20,000 postings.
The review audit retains 91.63% at 99.47% weak-label accuracy, not advisor accuracy.

9
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:20,000
The batch workflow loads the system once and preserves labels, review flags, actions,
policy reasons, and evidence for every row.

10
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:40,000
The completed package supports a human-supervised Career Center pilot.
Automated rejection, forwarding, hiring, or immigration decisions are not permitted.
